      "description": "The annex files themselves, as smart-base's `web-annex` kind (a WHO publication's web annexes, L1 or L2; owner, 2026-10-24, option A), which types them and judges them (`check:web-annexes`). `dak-data-dictionary.json` is Web Annex A of the IMMZ DAK (`annexOf` `who-iris/library/9789240099456-eng`, the held library entry of the DAK `dictionary.md` links to, IRIS 10665/380303; `section` `dak#core-data-elements`; no `iris` of its own, since none could be verified): the core data dictionary workbook (`input/L2/IMMZ DAK_core data dictionary.xlsx`) as `dak-data-dictionary/v1`, written by smart-base's `dak-data-dictionary.ts` (`--annex-of who-iris/library/9789240099456-eng --label \"Web Annex A\" --section dak#core-data-elements`). It records the workbook's sha256: regenerate it, never edit it. It is a sibling of `annexes/` rather than sharing that directory, because each kind owns the `$schema` families of its own directory, and not nested inside it, because a declared directory inside another declared one fails `check:layout-norms` (no typology here declares `within`).",
